1
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:04,967
<i> You know, Sir, I feel that...</i>

2
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:06,733
<i> even if we caught Berdugo,</i>

3
00:00:06,867 --> 00:00:08,767
<i>his viciousness is still around.</i>

4
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:09,967
<i> That's him!</i>

5
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:11,367
<i> That's the real Berdugo.</i>

6
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:12,867
<i> He's Andrew's family.</i>

7
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,867
<i>- That's his brother-in-law.
- No.</i>

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,900
<i> We need solid evidence</i>

9
00:00:17,033 --> 00:00:18,533
<i>if we don't want Berdugo
to escape.</i>

10
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:20,867
<i>Andrew? I didn't expect
to see you here.</i>

11
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,567
<i>I came here to check on you,
Tomas.</i>

12
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:26,667
<i>Of course, after Berdugo
was caught, right?</i>

13
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:28,433
<i>That's very thoughtful of you,
Andrew...</i>

14
00:00:28,567 --> 00:00:29,533
<i> but I'm fine.</i>

15
00:00:29,667 --> 00:00:30,767
<i>Is there something
you're not telling me?</i>

16
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:32,600
<i> Let's just wait for Andrew.</i>

17
00:00:32,733 --> 00:00:34,267
<i>What does Andrew
have to do with this?</i>

18
00:00:34,433 --> 00:00:36,633
<i> He's getting evidence.</i>

19
00:00:36,767 --> 00:00:38,100
<i> What evidence?</i>

20
00:00:38,233 --> 00:00:39,500
<i>Do you still remember
the teddy bear...</i>

21
00:00:39,633 --> 00:00:40,900
<i> you would always show me?</i>

22
00:00:41,033 --> 00:00:42,400
<i> Is it still here?</i>

23
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:47,067
<i> [OBB]</i>

24
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:02,700
He still hasn't answered.

25
00:01:04,233 --> 00:01:07,767
[HEAVY MUSIC PLAYING]

26
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:21,733
“Blood is thicker than water?”

27
00:01:21,867 --> 00:01:23,700
What do you mean?

28
00:01:25,033 --> 00:01:27,433
Berdugo is Andrew's relative?

29
00:01:29,033 --> 00:01:31,067
Jin Ho, he still has
a few minutes.

30
00:01:31,767 --> 00:01:33,633
He hasn't broken the deal yet.

31
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:36,200
He'll come here soon.

32
00:01:36,333 --> 00:01:40,267
[HEAVY MUSIC CONTINUES]

33
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:46,433
Andrew...

34
00:01:46,567 --> 00:01:47,733
You didn't run away.

35
00:01:47,867 --> 00:01:49,367
I would never do that.

36
00:01:50,867 --> 00:01:53,400
I'm always on the side
of truth...

37
00:01:53,533 --> 00:01:55,867
even if my enemy is family.

38
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:00,433
Major...

39
00:02:01,267 --> 00:02:03,033
this is what we need.

40
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:06,667
Because Tomas Limjoco...

41
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:09,067
is the real Berdugo.

42
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:13,367
[HEAVY MUSIC CONTINUES]

43
00:02:26,567 --> 00:02:29,267
[VIDEO GAME SFX]

44
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:31,200
[KNOCK ON THE DOOR]

45
00:02:33,467 --> 00:02:35,033
Oh, Dad.

46
00:02:35,167 --> 00:02:36,033
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

47
00:02:36,167 --> 00:02:37,800
Why aren't you asleep yet?

48
00:02:37,933 --> 00:02:39,467
Mom said I still have
an hour to play

49
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:41,800
after my homework.

50
00:02:41,933 --> 00:02:44,100
Did your Uncle Andrew
drop by earlier?

51
00:02:44,233 --> 00:02:46,200
What did he want?

52
00:02:47,633 --> 00:02:50,000
<i> I forgot, Uncle.</i>

53
00:02:50,133 --> 00:02:52,700
<i>I haven't even watched
the video yet.</i>

54
00:02:58,933 --> 00:03:00,500
<i>It's okay. I'll check it first.</i>

55
00:03:00,633 --> 00:03:02,500
<i>But promise me
this stays between us.</i>

56
00:03:02,633 --> 00:03:04,067
<i> Don't tell your mom and dad.</i>

57
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:05,067
<i> Why?</i>

58
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:07,267
<i>Because I have a surprise
for them.</i>

59
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:09,867
[CHUCKLES PRETENTIOUSLY]
<i> Okay, Uncle. Sure.</i>

60
00:03:10,833 --> 00:03:13,400
He just said good night, Dad.

61
00:03:15,367 --> 00:03:16,600
Are you sure?

62
00:03:16,733 --> 00:03:18,100
Yes, Dad.

63
00:03:21,033 --> 00:03:22,467
All right.

64
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:23,933
Wrap it up, okay?

65
00:03:24,067 --> 00:03:25,133
Don't stay up late.

66
00:03:25,267 --> 00:03:26,400
Yes.

67
00:03:26,533 --> 00:03:28,633
- Good night.
- Good night, Dad.

68
00:03:28,767 --> 00:03:32,867
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

69
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:49,000
<i> The lies must end tonight!</i>

70
00:03:49,133 --> 00:03:51,900
<i>Tell your family
who you really are,</i>

71
00:03:52,033 --> 00:03:54,567
<i>that you're the leader
of a syndicate...</i>

72
00:03:54,733 --> 00:03:56,700
<i>and you are Berdugo!
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

73
00:03:56,833 --> 00:03:57,967
<i> You think they'll believe you?</i>

74
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:00,700
<i> I'm telling my children now!</i>

75
00:04:00,833 --> 00:04:02,467
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

76
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:05,033
[REBECCA GRUNTING]

77
00:04:05,167 --> 00:04:06,400
[THUDS]

78
00:04:06,533 --> 00:04:10,700
[REBECCA GROANING]

79
00:04:14,267 --> 00:04:18,633
[REBECCA GROANING]

80
00:04:18,767 --> 00:04:23,100
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

81
00:04:25,333 --> 00:04:27,267
He's a monster!

82
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:31,133
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

83
00:04:32,367 --> 00:04:35,233
Mom knows what happened
with Tomas.

84
00:04:35,700 --> 00:04:39,900
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

85
00:04:46,367 --> 00:04:48,400
Andrew...

86
00:04:48,533 --> 00:04:51,067
I know this is very hard
for you,

87
00:04:52,533 --> 00:04:54,500
but as an investigator,

88
00:04:54,633 --> 00:04:57,100
I just want to understand...

89
00:04:57,233 --> 00:05:00,467
what role your mother had
with Berdugo.

90
00:05:02,267 --> 00:05:03,900
But before that,

91
00:05:04,467 --> 00:05:07,333
we need to capture Berdugo.

92
00:05:08,667 --> 00:05:10,400
Especially now.

93
00:05:11,333 --> 00:05:13,200
It's dangerous...

94
00:05:13,333 --> 00:05:15,600
Sir Tomas still controls
the situation,

95
00:05:15,733 --> 00:05:18,833
especially at the rest house
where your mom is.

96
00:05:19,533 --> 00:05:21,600
Isn't he controlling
the people taking care

97
00:05:21,733 --> 00:05:24,433
of your Mommy Rebecca?

98
00:05:25,033 --> 00:05:27,800
I won't let that happen
to my family.

99
00:05:28,667 --> 00:05:30,600
I need to keep them safe!

100
00:05:32,733 --> 00:05:34,767
But how?

101
00:05:37,167 --> 00:05:40,867
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

102
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,833
I have an idea...

103
00:05:43,867 --> 00:05:46,267
but, I'll need help with this.

104
00:05:53,367 --> 00:05:55,100
At last,<i> Tirada</i> enjoyers.

105
00:05:55,233 --> 00:05:59,700
We've tracked down the notorious
drug supplier, Berdugo.

106
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:02,433
[GALVANIZING MUSIC PLAYING]

107
00:06:02,567 --> 00:06:06,000
Despite hiding behind
a legitimate business,

108
00:06:06,133 --> 00:06:08,633
the truth has come out, Tirada.

109
00:06:09,167 --> 00:06:15,333
Matias is indeed the head
of that illegal operation.

110
00:06:15,733 --> 00:06:20,267
We witnessed the dangers
faced by the police.

111
00:06:20,633 --> 00:06:25,433
And now, we can say it's over.

112
00:06:26,033 --> 00:06:30,233
This chaos is over,

113
00:06:30,367 --> 00:06:33,467
and Berdugo is behind bars.

114
00:06:34,367 --> 00:06:36,533
So, congratulations
to Bolagos Police

115
00:06:36,667 --> 00:06:40,667
for a job well done
and to all agencies involved,

116
00:06:41,133 --> 00:06:44,700
especially Major Miguel Delgado
and Unit 2.

117
00:06:44,833 --> 00:06:47,067
Until next time,
<i> Tirada</i> listeners.

118
00:06:49,033 --> 00:06:50,700
Cut.

119
00:06:51,367 --> 00:06:52,733
Andrew...

120
00:06:52,867 --> 00:06:53,967
when did you become a parrot?

121
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:56,400
That's the same report
everyone else gave.

122
00:06:56,533 --> 00:06:57,733
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

123
00:06:57,867 --> 00:06:58,900
The numbers are low.

124
00:06:59,033 --> 00:07:00,333
What?

125
00:07:00,467 --> 00:07:02,267
The number of viewers is low
during our live,

126
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:07,100
and as it went on,
engagement kept dropping.

127
00:07:07,233 --> 00:07:08,533
Really?

128
00:07:08,667 --> 00:07:10,800
I'm more surprised
anyone stayed.

129
00:07:10,933 --> 00:07:12,700
Well, how could they?
It was basic.

130
00:07:12,833 --> 00:07:14,500
Lacking insight.

131
00:07:14,667 --> 00:07:17,033
Exactly, here,
I'll read the comments.

132
00:07:17,167 --> 00:07:17,967
This one says...

133
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:19,867
“The report was boring,

134
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,967
so watching was boring too.”

135
00:07:22,100 --> 00:07:24,033
Here's another...

136
00:07:24,167 --> 00:07:26,467
“Your Boss Idol is tired.”

137
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:27,500
Ouch.

138
00:07:27,633 --> 00:07:29,000
With a crying emoji.

139
00:07:29,133 --> 00:07:30,533
Another one...

140
00:07:30,667 --> 00:07:33,133
“He's ran out of guts already?”

141
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,800
Just chill.

142
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:38,000
It's all part of the plan.

143
00:07:38,133 --> 00:07:39,933
What plan?

144
00:07:40,067 --> 00:07:44,000
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

145
00:07:44,133 --> 00:07:46,867
<i>The truth has come out,
Tirada enjoyers.</i>

146
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:51,967
<i>Matias is indeed the head
of that illegal operation.</i>

147
00:07:52,133 --> 00:07:54,967
[PHONE RINGS]

148
00:07:55,100 --> 00:07:56,933
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

149
00:07:57,067 --> 00:07:58,000
Yes?

150
00:07:58,133 --> 00:08:00,900
<i>Berdugo, it's quiet here
at the precinct.</i>

151
00:08:01,033 --> 00:08:03,533
<i>No one's moving
among Delgado's men.</i>

152
00:08:03,667 --> 00:08:05,867
<i>Matias's arraignment
is proceeding.</i>

153
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,233
<i>He'll be transferred
to the provincial jail.</i>

154
00:08:08,367 --> 00:08:11,200
<i>Looks like you have nothing
to worry about, Berdugo.</i>

155
00:08:11,333 --> 00:08:13,833
Okay, just stay alert.

156
00:08:13,967 --> 00:08:15,500
<i> Always, Boss.</i>

157
00:08:15,633 --> 00:08:19,667
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

158
00:08:20,533 --> 00:08:22,700
We'll see grandmother again!

159
00:08:22,867 --> 00:08:23,467
Yay!

160
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:25,067
Just be a good girl, okay?

161
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:26,367
Yes, Mommy.
[CHUCKLES]

162
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:28,567
- You too.
- Yes.

163
00:08:28,700 --> 00:08:30,233
What's going on?

164
00:08:33,133 --> 00:08:36,500
We're going to the rest house
to visit mommy.

165
00:08:36,633 --> 00:08:39,567
She's getting better,
but if the kids visit her,

166
00:08:39,700 --> 00:08:42,933
it could help her more.

167
00:08:43,067 --> 00:08:45,767
But we'll be back tonight.

168
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:49,967
I'll go with you guys.

169
00:08:50,100 --> 00:08:52,400
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

170
00:08:52,533 --> 00:08:54,833
You're coming?

171
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:57,133
Yes, I want to be with you.

172
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:59,233
Daddy's coming too?

173
00:08:59,367 --> 00:09:00,833
Yay!

174
00:09:02,833 --> 00:09:05,167
Okay, let's go.

175
00:09:05,300 --> 00:09:09,900
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

176
00:09:15,467 --> 00:09:17,333
[PHONE CHIMES]

177
00:09:17,933 --> 00:09:21,933
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

178
00:09:32,067 --> 00:09:33,800
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

179
00:09:33,933 --> 00:09:35,500
Are you okay?

180
00:09:37,233 --> 00:09:39,500
Tomas went with Yvette.

181
00:09:42,067 --> 00:09:43,967
Oh, no!

182
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:46,100
He knows.

183
00:09:46,233 --> 00:09:48,700
Maybe he just wants family time.

184
00:09:48,833 --> 00:09:52,833
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

185
00:09:56,300 --> 00:09:58,567
Major, this is Andrew.

186
00:09:58,700 --> 00:10:00,167
<i> There's been a change.</i>

187
00:10:00,300 --> 00:10:04,100
Tomas went with Yvette
to the rest house.

188
00:10:04,267 --> 00:10:05,900
Copy!
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

189
00:10:06,033 --> 00:10:07,600
Andrew...

190
00:10:07,733 --> 00:10:10,100
<i>tell Yvette to go straight
to the rest house.</i>

191
00:10:10,233 --> 00:10:12,733
After that, we'll handle it.

192
00:10:13,333 --> 00:10:15,000
<i> All units, change of plan!</i>

193
00:10:15,133 --> 00:10:17,300
<i>We're heading straight
to the rest house.</i>

194
00:10:17,433 --> 00:10:19,200
Secure the Dizons.

195
00:10:20,233 --> 00:10:22,300
I'll take care of Berdugo.

196
00:10:22,433 --> 00:10:24,467
Loud and clear, Sir.

197
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:27,433
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

198
00:10:45,433 --> 00:10:47,600
Major, what I feared
has already happened.

199
00:10:47,733 --> 00:10:49,200
<i> My family is in danger now</i>

200
00:10:49,333 --> 00:10:51,167
<i> because Tomas went with them.</i>

201
00:10:51,733 --> 00:10:53,900
Major, this wasn't our plan.

202
00:10:54,033 --> 00:10:56,433
<i>I know, Andrew, it's hard
to control the situation.</i>

203
00:10:56,567 --> 00:10:58,733
But let's plan it carefully.

204
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:00,833
Just trust us.

205
00:11:05,967 --> 00:11:07,767
<i> We can't move...</i>

206
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:10,800
<i>until we're sure
your family is safe.</i>

207
00:11:10,967 --> 00:11:13,100
<i> We know what Tomas can do...</i>

208
00:11:13,867 --> 00:11:15,700
<i>even to the people close to him.</i>

209
00:11:15,833 --> 00:11:19,067
<i>That's why we need to put
your family in a safe place,</i>

210
00:11:19,967 --> 00:11:22,333
<i> before we capture Berdugo.</i>

211
00:11:22,467 --> 00:11:25,467
<i>But, Dad, what if
he already has an idea?</i>

212
00:11:33,500 --> 00:11:35,000
<i> And if he suspects anything,</i>

213
00:11:35,133 --> 00:11:36,233
<i> he won't leave his family.</i>

214
00:11:36,367 --> 00:11:37,633
<i> He'll guard them.</i>

215
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:46,233
<i>That's why we need
to get ahead of him.</i>

216
00:11:49,433 --> 00:11:51,033
<i> That can only happen...</i>

217
00:11:51,167 --> 00:11:52,967
<i>if Yvette knows what's going on.</i>

218
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:54,800
<i> She has more leverage.</i>

219
00:11:54,933 --> 00:11:56,700
<i> She can help us.</i>

220
00:11:57,367 --> 00:12:00,267
[SOBBING]

221
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:04,233
[REBECCA GROANING IN VIDEO]

222
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:10,867
<i> Andrew...</i>

223
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,233
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

224
00:12:12,367 --> 00:12:15,200
<i>This isn't true, Andrew,
this isn't true.</i>

225
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:18,667
<i>I'm sorry, Yvette,
but we don't have time.</i>

226
00:12:19,567 --> 00:12:21,400
<i> We need to act now.</i>

227
00:12:22,833 --> 00:12:25,167
<i> I know it's painful, but...</i>

228
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:29,833
<i>we can't let anyone else
in our family get hurt.</i>

229
00:12:29,967 --> 00:12:32,167
<i>Yvette, we need to be strong,
okay?</i>

230
00:12:33,700 --> 00:12:35,267
<i> For mommy.</i>

231
00:12:36,667 --> 00:12:38,633
<i> For your kids.</i>

232
00:12:38,767 --> 00:12:41,567
<i> Please, Yvette,</i>

233
00:12:41,700 --> 00:12:44,433
<i>don't say mention anything
to Tomas about this.</i>

234
00:12:44,567 --> 00:12:47,667
<i>He must not get any hint
that we know.</i>

235
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:49,533
<i> How can I do that?</i>

236
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:51,233
<i> I can't.</i>

237
00:12:51,367 --> 00:12:53,867
<i> I can't, Andrew.</i>

238
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:55,967
<i> Yvette, you have to, please.</i>

239
00:12:56,633 --> 00:13:00,800
<i>He's not the same person
we thought he was.</i>

240
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:03,300
<i> Yvette, he must not find out</i>

241
00:13:03,433 --> 00:13:05,300
<i>that we already know everything.</i>

242
00:13:05,433 --> 00:13:06,667
<i> Otherwise, even Harris,</i>

243
00:13:06,800 --> 00:13:09,767
<i>the kids could get
dragged into this.</i>

244
00:13:09,900 --> 00:13:11,733
<i>Yvette, I'm not trying
to scare you,</i>

245
00:13:12,733 --> 00:13:16,067
<i>but we need to prepare
for the worst.</i>

246
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:19,133
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

247
00:13:19,267 --> 00:13:21,567
<i>And this is how
we protect our family.</i>

248
00:13:22,500 --> 00:13:27,000
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

249
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,300
<i> Yes.</i>

250
00:13:34,133 --> 00:13:35,233
<i> All right, Andrew.</i>

251
00:13:35,367 --> 00:13:37,000
<i> Tell me...</i>

252
00:13:38,233 --> 00:13:40,600
<i> what I need to do.</i>

253
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:45,300
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

254
00:13:47,433 --> 00:13:51,367
[REVVING]

255
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:55,533
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

256
00:14:11,767 --> 00:14:15,433
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

257
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:26,100
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

258
00:14:42,333 --> 00:14:46,600
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

259
00:14:51,933 --> 00:14:56,000
Hon, we're here.

260
00:14:56,567 --> 00:14:59,300
I was just thinking
if I forgot something.

261
00:15:02,833 --> 00:15:04,167
Let's go, kids.

262
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:05,667
[PHONE CHIMES]

263
00:15:06,800 --> 00:15:10,367
[PHONE KEYS CLICKING]

264
00:15:11,633 --> 00:15:15,667
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

265
00:15:20,167 --> 00:15:21,633
Who are you texting?

266
00:15:24,400 --> 00:15:25,700
It's Andrew.

267
00:15:26,167 --> 00:15:27,933
I'm just texting him.

268
00:15:28,067 --> 00:15:31,133
I asked him to come here
so he can join us.

269
00:15:36,033 --> 00:15:38,467
I missed you!

270
00:15:44,267 --> 00:15:48,300
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

271
00:15:54,033 --> 00:15:56,167
Sir, what if Tomas already knows

272
00:15:56,300 --> 00:15:58,267
that we know he's Berdugo?

273
00:15:59,133 --> 00:16:00,267
What do you mean?

274
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:02,167
He was tipped off
before we entered?

275
00:16:02,300 --> 00:16:03,567
Isn't that possible, Sir?

276
00:16:03,700 --> 00:16:05,800
We already caught Salazar

277
00:16:05,933 --> 00:16:07,500
before he could tip him off.

278
00:16:07,633 --> 00:16:09,300
He has no eyes on us anymore.

279
00:16:09,467 --> 00:16:12,700
So, let's just focus
on how we'll get the Dizons out.

280
00:16:13,200 --> 00:16:15,333
- Yvette!
- How are you, Mom?

281
00:16:15,467 --> 00:16:16,533
Okay, I'm fine.

282
00:16:16,667 --> 00:16:18,667
Mommy, are you taking
your medicine?

283
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:19,800
Of course.

284
00:16:19,933 --> 00:16:21,800
Is mommy a good girl, Nanny?

285
00:16:21,933 --> 00:16:23,500
Wow! Good girl.

286
00:16:23,633 --> 00:16:25,133
Oh, don't you want to swim?

287
00:16:25,267 --> 00:16:27,033
She's excited to swim, Mom.

288
00:16:27,167 --> 00:16:28,433
Oh, it's clean!

289
00:16:28,567 --> 00:16:29,967
They cleaned the pool!

290
00:16:30,100 --> 00:16:31,433
It's waiting for you!

291
00:16:31,567 --> 00:16:32,567
See?

292
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:34,267
It's so exciting.

293
00:16:36,267 --> 00:16:40,433
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

294
00:16:47,467 --> 00:16:48,900
Listen up!

295
00:16:49,033 --> 00:16:50,067
Secure the perimeter.

296
00:16:50,200 --> 00:16:52,733
No one goes in or out.

297
00:16:52,867 --> 00:16:55,900
Major, Yvette told me
there are many armed guards.

298
00:16:56,033 --> 00:16:57,433
Oh, take note!

299
00:17:00,867 --> 00:17:02,233
Andrew...

300
00:17:02,367 --> 00:17:03,433
you will go in first.

301
00:17:03,567 --> 00:17:05,000
Bring your car.

302
00:17:05,533 --> 00:17:07,100
Secure your family.

303
00:17:07,500 --> 00:17:08,933
Prioritize the kids.

304
00:17:09,533 --> 00:17:12,133
Joey, you'll meet them.

305
00:17:12,267 --> 00:17:13,967
Bring them here.

306
00:17:14,100 --> 00:17:15,467
- Okay?
- Yes, Dad.

307
00:17:15,633 --> 00:17:17,967
Jin Ho, you are coming with me.

308
00:17:18,100 --> 00:17:21,267
You'll identify
if Tomas is indeed Berdugo.

309
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:22,633
Copy, Sir.

310
00:17:22,767 --> 00:17:24,433
We'll move in two minutes!

311
00:17:24,567 --> 00:17:26,233
Sir, comms check.

312
00:17:26,833 --> 00:17:27,800
Check.

313
00:17:27,933 --> 00:17:29,067
Check.

314
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:31,233
- Check.
- Check.

315
00:17:32,767 --> 00:17:35,167
Joey, stay in the van.

316
00:17:35,300 --> 00:17:37,333
Don't get out
until the Dizons arrive.

317
00:17:37,467 --> 00:17:38,467
All right.

318
00:17:38,600 --> 00:17:39,467
Be careful, Dad.

319
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:40,633
Thank you.

320
00:17:40,767 --> 00:17:42,433
Boys, positions!

321
00:17:42,567 --> 00:17:46,767
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

322
00:17:50,633 --> 00:17:53,167
[ENGINE STARTS]

323
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:57,867
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

324
00:17:58,133 --> 00:18:00,067
So, kids, after you swim,

325
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:01,933
go out to grandmother's garden,
okay?

326
00:18:02,067 --> 00:18:03,733
You can spend time with her.

327
00:18:03,867 --> 00:18:06,667
Grandmother can play with us?

328
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:09,800
But didn't you say you don't
want her going outside, Mommy?

329
00:18:09,933 --> 00:18:13,900
You said it's not safe for her
to be seen by other people.

330
00:18:14,033 --> 00:18:17,067
You could, just for today.
It's okay.

331
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:18,567
Right, Mom?

332
00:18:20,167 --> 00:18:22,567
Well, whatever you say.

333
00:18:22,733 --> 00:18:24,133
Isn't it hot outside?

334
00:18:25,300 --> 00:18:27,033
It'll just be for a while, Hon.

335
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:29,133
It's good for mommy, too...

336
00:18:29,267 --> 00:18:32,400
so she can breathe fresh air.

337
00:18:34,767 --> 00:18:35,600
Ma'am...

338
00:18:35,733 --> 00:18:36,800
your basket is ready.

339
00:18:36,933 --> 00:18:37,800
It's with the guard.

340
00:18:37,933 --> 00:18:39,033
Why?

341
00:18:39,167 --> 00:18:42,867
Because you always go straight
there when you come here.

342
00:18:45,033 --> 00:18:47,667
Oh, yes. Maybe next time.

343
00:18:47,800 --> 00:18:49,667
I want to spend time with them.

344
00:18:50,567 --> 00:18:51,833
Right?

345
00:18:52,833 --> 00:18:54,300
<i> Okay.</i>

346
00:18:55,567 --> 00:18:59,667
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

347
00:19:01,567 --> 00:19:03,467
I'm sorry. Oh, sorry.

348
00:19:04,233 --> 00:19:06,567
Mom, you keep dropping it!

349
00:19:06,700 --> 00:19:10,667
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

350
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:21,700
[CAR HONKING]

351
00:19:22,333 --> 00:19:24,100
[CAR HONKING]

352
00:19:25,467 --> 00:19:27,000
Why are there no guards here?

353
00:19:27,133 --> 00:19:32,167
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

354
00:19:43,233 --> 00:19:46,833
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

355
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:55,300
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

356
00:20:08,567 --> 00:20:12,933
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

357
00:20:18,633 --> 00:20:23,200
[PHONE RINGING]

358
00:20:23,333 --> 00:20:26,733
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

359
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:35,833
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

360
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,067
<i> I'm sorry, the subscriber...</i>

361
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:47,933
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

362
00:20:58,333 --> 00:21:02,333
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

363
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:06,433
[KNOCKING]

364
00:21:06,567 --> 00:21:09,500
<i> Yvette! Yvette!</i>

365
00:21:09,667 --> 00:21:13,433
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

366
00:21:30,067 --> 00:21:31,133
Andrew, why?

367
00:21:31,267 --> 00:21:32,867
<i> Major, the house is locked.</i>

368
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:34,633
It looks like no one's inside.

369
00:21:34,767 --> 00:21:36,233
No one's answering.

370
00:21:36,367 --> 00:21:37,500
We have to check now.

371
00:21:37,633 --> 00:21:38,600
Wait, Major.

372
00:21:38,733 --> 00:21:40,567
I'll take a look around first,
okay?

373
00:21:40,700 --> 00:21:42,067
Copy.

374
00:21:47,767 --> 00:21:49,467
- Miss...
- Sir Andrew!

375
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:50,533
What happened?

376
00:21:50,667 --> 00:21:51,833
Sir...

377
00:21:51,967 --> 00:21:53,833
Where are Yvette and the others?

378
00:21:54,433 --> 00:21:58,967
They're inside,
but Sir Tomas has a gun.

379
00:21:59,100 --> 00:22:01,133
He won't let them out.

380
00:22:03,500 --> 00:22:06,400
Major, Yvette and the others
are inside.

381
00:22:06,933 --> 00:22:09,300
Tomas won't let them out.
He has a gun.

382
00:22:09,433 --> 00:22:10,467
Don't go in.

383
00:22:10,600 --> 00:22:12,100
Wait for us.

384
00:22:13,300 --> 00:22:14,767
Come here.

385
00:22:17,033 --> 00:22:18,500
Let's move!

386
00:22:18,633 --> 00:22:22,600
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

387
00:22:30,900 --> 00:22:31,867
What's the situation inside?

388
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:33,067
Sir...

389
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:36,133
Sir Tomas is armed.

390
00:22:36,267 --> 00:22:37,967
I'm here now.
I'm with Elai.

391
00:22:38,100 --> 00:22:39,233
How are you all there?
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

392
00:22:39,367 --> 00:22:41,767
I'm just waiting for Andrew
to get his family out.

393
00:22:43,967 --> 00:22:45,800
[MOUTHS "COVER"]

394
00:22:45,933 --> 00:22:49,133
[GUN FIRING]

395
00:22:50,233 --> 00:22:51,200
[BULLET PLINKS]

396
00:22:51,333 --> 00:22:52,567
Ma'am, don't go out, okay?

397
00:22:52,700 --> 00:22:53,633
Stay here.

398
00:22:53,767 --> 00:22:55,833
Joey, what's that?
Is there a shootout?

399
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:59,800
[GUN FIRING]

400
00:23:00,400 --> 00:23:03,700
[GUN FIRING]

401
00:23:04,300 --> 00:23:06,600
[GUN FIRING]

402
00:23:07,567 --> 00:23:11,600
[GUN FIRING]
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

403
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:16,133
[GUN FIRING]

404
00:23:17,133 --> 00:23:19,900
[GUN FIRING]

405
00:23:25,800 --> 00:23:27,500
Dad...

406
00:23:28,367 --> 00:23:32,767
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

407
00:23:35,700 --> 00:23:37,367
I'm here at Berdugo's
rest house.

408
00:23:37,500 --> 00:23:38,500
I'll try to get them out.

409
00:23:38,633 --> 00:23:39,700
I just need help.

410
00:23:39,833 --> 00:23:41,467
This is good,
the connection stable.

411
00:23:41,600 --> 00:23:43,067
Andrew said we're
about to start.

412
00:23:43,200 --> 00:23:46,800
<i>I need a vehicle with two
fully loaded long arms.</i>

413
00:23:46,933 --> 00:23:49,267
If anyone disobeys,
someone will die here.

414
00:23:49,400 --> 00:23:51,800
How long will you hide
behind your hostages?

415
00:23:51,933 --> 00:23:53,667
Is that the Berdugo
everyone fears?

416
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:55,933
How dare you betray me?

417
00:23:56,100 --> 00:23:57,700
Did you think
I wouldn't sense it?

418
00:23:57,833 --> 00:23:59,067
It's time we execute plan B.

419
00:23:59,200 --> 00:24:00,100
I have an idea.

420
00:24:00,233 --> 00:24:01,667
I'll only talk to you.

421
00:24:01,800 --> 00:24:04,267
If I hear even
the slightest noise,

422
00:24:04,400 --> 00:24:05,900
somebody will die.
